From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] greeter: one left edge for the input fields

VALUE_X placed each input field after its own prompt, measured as the
larger of the default prompts' widths and the current prompt's.  SetPrompt
pads the current prompt to two trailing spaces, so "password: " became
one space wider than the default prompts and the password field started a
space to the right of the name field.  Both fields now start after the
wider of the two current prompts.
---
 greeter/Login.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/greeter/Login.c b/greeter/Login.c
index 408c26f..2fe9dde 100644
--- a/greeter/Login.c
+++ b/greeter/Login.c
@@ -331,7 +331,11 @@ XmuXftTextWidth(Display *dpy, XftFont *font, FcChar8 *string, int len);
 			 (n * PROMPT_SPACE_Y(w)))
 #define PROMPT_W(w)	(w->core.width - (2 * TEXT_X_INC(w)))
 #define PROMPT_H(w)	(5 * Y_INC(w) / 4)
-#define VALUE_X(w,n)	(PROMPT_X(w) + CUR_PROMPT_W(w,n))
+/* every input field starts at the same x, after the wider of the current
+   prompts (SetPrompt pads each to two trailing spaces, so a prompt can be
+   wider than the default prompts that CUR_PROMPT_W compares it with) */
+#define MAX_CUR_PROMPT_W(w)	(max(CUR_PROMPT_W(w,0), CUR_PROMPT_W(w,1)))
+#define VALUE_X(w,n)	(PROMPT_X(w) + MAX_CUR_PROMPT_W(w))
 #define CURSOR_W	5
 #define MAX_VALUE_W(w,n) (PROMPT_W(w) - VALUE_X (w,n) - CURSOR_W - 1 - \
 			  (w->login.inframeswidth * 2) - LOGO_W(w))
